{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/365","id":4718684889,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGUFq2Q","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/365","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/365.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/365.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/365","number":365,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[2303002] Credited harmonic-path resolution (already solved, 0/5)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accept the credited resolution of Hayman–Lingham Problem 3.2 as `already_solved, 0/5`. For every finite real nonconstant harmonic function on all of R^n, n >= 3, the packet proves a continuous, spatially locally finite polygonal path whose entire tail escapes every compact set and along which the function tends to positive infinity. The original [Update 3.2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1809.07200), printed page 60, already records the affirmative result and credits prior work; [Carleson (1976)](https://www.acadsci.fi/mathematica/Vol02/vol02pp035-039.pdf), pages 35–39, gives the polygonal strengthening. This is source-credited proof verification, with no novel theorem claimed.\n\nThe full analytic proof was reviewed independently before program execution by ROOT, two distinct approach families, and a fresh whole-packet adversary. The normalized Poisson comparison, zero-pasting across arbitrary component boundaries, obstruction to two bounded-value components, choice through infinitely many possible children, one-sided harmonic Liouville including zero-center values, and whole-tail properness all check. Complete author and portable verification outputs reproduce byte-for-byte (3,675 author controls; 1,667 with the two primary PDF identities, or 1,665 in math-only mode). ROOT also verified every original Git/API/disk binding and all 29 nested manifest instances, the actual ten-file source checkpoint and preserved ancestry, and reexecuted all 69 read-only family commands with complete output comparisons. Symbolic and adverse controls supplement the analytic proof; their finite success does not establish the continuum theorem.\n\nOnly this problem's queue status changes to `already_solved`; its genuine discovery-turn count remains `0/5`, and all 18 mathematical packet files are unchanged. The historical unavailable dataset revision and broad search counts are not newly certified. The discontinuous-subharmonic extension, prescribed rays, quantitative rates, monotone values, injectivity and finite total length are outside the independently verified scope. The source's apparent thinness-sign typo is not used in this elementary proof. The current whole-review verifier documents the historical family verifiers' private-evidence requirements and strengthens public inventory checks; immutable review seals and complete local evidence are preserved.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in deriving and auditing the packet. These independent AI reviews are unrefereed and are not a claim of human peer review. Acceptance publishes the valid credited findings under the requested partial-result process. No research paper, preprint, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker entry or release is created for this `already_solved` result. Audit evidence is under `draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr365_2303002/`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:10:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T19:37:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ecd66e416130a840a9d3756c88e2549af398575d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/365/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/365/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/365/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/47dbe2c144a77f590faf144b950f1e759db92e75","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-2303002","ref":"dot/math-2303002","sha":"47dbe2c144a77f590faf144b950f1e759db92e75","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received